<div class="sop-meta">
  <div><strong>Trigger</strong> Sign-off received from QA phase</div>
  <div><strong>Owner</strong> Lead developer + lead owner (handles client comms)</div>
  <div><strong>Time</strong> 30-90 min active work + monitoring through 24 hours after</div>
  <div><strong>Output</strong> Live site at the client's real domain, monitoring active, owner's guide delivered</div>
</div>

<h2>Pick the launch window</h2>
<p>Tuesday-Thursday morning Mountain Time is ideal. Avoid:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Friday afternoons (weekend issues compound)</li>
  <li>Mondays (catch-up day, distractions)</li>
  <li>Days before holidays</li>
  <li>Dates the client has out-of-office</li>
  <li>Dates with known industry traffic spikes (storm season, peak booking)</li>
</ul>

<h2>30 minutes before launch</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Re-run Lighthouse on the preview URL. Save scores for the post-launch comparison.</li>
  <li>Confirm DNS TTL is dropped to 5 minutes (do this 24-48 hours before to make rollback fast if needed).</li>
  <li>Verify the production Cloudflare Pages project has the right environment variables (form keys, analytics IDs).</li>
  <li>Have the client's domain registrar dashboard open in another tab.</li>
  <li>Open monitoring tools (Cloudflare status, UptimeRobot dashboard).</li>
  <li>Notify client launch starts in 30 min.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The launch itself</h2>

<h3>Step 1: connect the custom domain (5 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>In the Cloudflare Pages project, add the client's domain as a custom domain.</li>
  <li>Cloudflare provisions an SSL cert and gives the CNAME / A record values.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 2: update DNS at the registrar (5-10 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>If client uses Cloudflare nameservers: update DNS records directly in Cloudflare.</li>
  <li>If client stays at their registrar: have them (or you, with their permission) update the A / CNAME / AAAA records to point at Cloudflare Pages.</li>
  <li>Preserve MX, TXT (SPF/DKIM/DMARC), and any other non-A records. We're only updating where the website points, not email.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 3: verify propagation (5-15 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Use <code>dig +short {domain}</code> from terminal. Should return Cloudflare's IPs.</li>
  <li>Test the live URL in a fresh browser (incognito). HTTPS works, content loads.</li>
  <li>If you previously dropped TTL to 5 min, propagation is usually under 10 min globally.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 4: verify SSL + redirects (5 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>HTTPS works without warning.</li>
  <li>HTTP redirects to HTTPS automatically (Cloudflare default).</li>
  <li>www.domain.com and domain.com both resolve (canonical URL set in Cloudflare).</li>
  <li><code>curl -sI https://{domain}/</code> returns expected headers (HSTS, CSP, X-Frame-Options).</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 5: post-launch QA (10 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Click through the navigation: header, footer, mobile nav.</li>
  <li>Submit a real form (use a +launchtest@ email alias). Verify it lands in client inbox.</li>
  <li>Open on a real phone via cellular (not WiFi).</li>
  <li>Open in 2-3 different browsers.</li>
  <li>Check the search modal works.</li>
  <li>Check the theme toggle works + persists.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 6: SEO + analytics (5 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Submit the new sitemap to Google Search Console: <code>https://{domain}/sitemap.xml</code>.</li>
  <li>If client has an existing Search Console property, verify the new sitemap shows up there.</li>
  <li>Submit to Bing Webmaster Tools (still ~10-15% of US service-business search).</li>
  <li>Configure Cloudflare Web Analytics on the new domain if not already.</li>
  <li>If the client has Umami: confirm tracking script is firing.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 7: monitoring on (5 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Add the production URL to UptimeRobot. 1-min check interval. SMS alerts to the on-call number.</li>
  <li>Verify Cloudflare uptime monitoring is on.</li>
  <li>Add domain to WHOIS-watch list for renewal monitoring.</li>
  <li>Cloudflare Pages keeps every prior deploy; bookmark the dashboard for one-click rollback if needed.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Step 8: hand over the owner's guide (10 min)</h3>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Send the launch confirmation email below.</li>
  <li>Link to the public <a href="/owners-guide/">/owners-guide/</a>.</li>
  <li>Send a personalized version with their actual subprocessors, hosting account, etc. (private Notion / PDF).</li>
  <li>Confirm what email address gets form submissions.</li>
</ul>

