<h2>The next 24 hours</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Check Cloudflare analytics 2-3 times: traffic, error rate, bot activity.</li>
  <li>Watch UptimeRobot for any flaps.</li>
  <li>Re-run Lighthouse on the live URL: scores should match preview within 2-3 points.</li>
  <li>If client reports any issue, respond within an hour.</li>
  <li>End of day: send "all good" check-in if you haven't heard from them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The first week</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Day 3: check Search Console for crawl errors. Should be zero.</li>
  <li>Day 5: submit any high-value pages individually for crawling (homepage, top service pages).</li>
  <li>Day 7: send a 1-week check-in. Ask if anything's come up.</li>
  <li>Confirm form submissions are arriving (ask client directly).</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common launch issues</h2>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>DNS won't propagate</strong>
  Verify TTL was dropped pre-launch. Use <code>dig +short {domain}</code> from multiple regions (or whatsmydns.net). Most "DNS issues" are caching at the user's ISP; affected user just needs to wait or flush DNS.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>HTTPS shows certificate warning</strong>
  Cloudflare's managed cert can take 5-15 min to provision. If still failing after 30 min, check that the domain is correctly added in Cloudflare Pages and that the registrar's records match what Cloudflare expects.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Old site still showing for the client</strong>
  Their browser cached the old DNS. Have them flush DNS cache or test in incognito. Within 24 hours, propagation completes globally.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Form submissions not arriving</strong>
  Check Web3Forms dashboard for the access key. Check the <code>action</code> URL in the form. Test from a fresh browser without ad blockers.
</div>

<div class="sop-callout sop-callout--warn">
  <strong>Search Console errors immediately after launch</strong>
  Normal. Some errors take 24-72 hours to clear as Google re-crawls. Investigate if errors persist past 7 days.
</div>

<h2>Exit criteria</h2>
<p>Live site verified working at the production domain. SSL active. Sitemap submitted. Monitoring on. Owner's guide handed over. Client confirmed they can reach the site. Move to <a href="/sop/maintenance/">phase 09</a> (ongoing).</p>
